---
import BinderLayout from '../layouts/BinderLayout.astro';
---

<BinderLayout
    title="Scroll test | Kevin"
    description="A manual test for the scrolling paper and stationary binder navigation."
    noindex
>
    <article class="scroll-test">
        <section class="checkpoint" aria-labelledby="test-start">
            <p class="checkpoint-label">01 / Top of the paper</p>
            <h1 id="test-start">Scroll test</h1>
            <p>
                This page has three screens of content and uses the same binder layout as the
                portfolio.
            </p>
            <ol>
                <li>Place your pointer over the paper and scroll down slowly.</li>
                <li>Watch a horizontal grid line: it should move with the text.</li>
                <li>The dark navigation bar and its rounded corner should stay in place.</li>
            </ol>
            <p>
                To test the top edge, scroll upward here and release. Any elastic bounce should stay
                inside the paper area.
            </p>
            <p>
                Use a trackpad or touch screen to check the bounce; its appearance depends on your
                browser and device.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="checkpoint" aria-labelledby="test-middle">
            <p class="checkpoint-label">02 / Middle of the paper</p>
            <h3 id="test-middle">Keep scrolling</h3>
            <p>The heading and grid should travel together beneath the navigation.</p>
            <p>The red margin line should continue for the full length of the paper.</p>
            <p>
                Try reversing direction halfway through a scroll. The navigation should remain in
                the same place.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="checkpoint checkpoint-end" aria-labelledby="test-end">
            <p class="checkpoint-label">03 / Bottom of the paper</p>
            <h3 id="test-end">Scroll a little further, then release</h3>
            <p>
                You have reached the end. Keep scrolling downward briefly, then lift your fingers.
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>The navigation should stay still throughout the gesture.</li>
                <li>On devices with elastic scrolling, the paper should bounce and settle.</li>
                <li>Watch for an exposed blank strip or a frozen grid during the bounce.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                Scroll back to the top to test the other edge, or <a href="/">return home</a>.
            </p>
            <p class="end-marker">End of test content</p>
        </section>
    </article>
</BinderLayout>

<style>
    /* ======================================================================
       Diagnostic page layout
       ====================================================================== */
    .scroll-test {
        color: var(--black-ink-color);
        font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
        line-height: var(--scroll-test-line-height);
    }

    .checkpoint {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: flex-start;
        min-height: var(--scroll-test-checkpoint-min-height);
        padding: var(--scroll-test-checkpoint-padding-block)
            clamp(
                var(--scroll-test-checkpoint-padding-inline-min),
                var(--scroll-test-checkpoint-padding-inline-fluid),
                var(--scroll-test-checkpoint-padding-inline-max)
            );
    }

    .checkpoint > * {
        max-width: var(--scroll-test-content-max-width);
    }

    .checkpoint-label,
    .end-marker {
        font-weight: 700;
    }

    .checkpoint-end {
        justify-content: flex-end;
    }

    .end-marker {
        align-self: stretch;
        margin-bottom: 0;
        border-top: var(--scroll-test-marker-width) solid var(--margin-color);
        padding-top: var(--scroll-test-end-marker-padding-top);
    }
</style>
